WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
[ Music ]

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:26.320
[Narrator:] The physician has always regarded 
house calls as a part of his duty to his patients.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:35.000
And for years, nursing service has been available to patients at home through public health departments

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.700
and visiting nurse associations.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:44.700
[ Music ]

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.760
[Narrator:] Physical and occupational therapists, too, have made their services available

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:50.440
to invalids in their homes.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:55.900
[ Music ]

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:59.060
[Narrator:] Recently, a new member of the medical team has made it possible

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:02.500
to offer more extensive home care to patients.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:07.000
This is the home health aide.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:51.840
[ Music ]

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:56.500
[Narrator:] Anyone in the community might someday need the services of the home health 
aide.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:02.900
A typical story might begin here, or here in a hospital.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:09.200
Before the home health aide begins her job, a referral must first be made by the patient's physician

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.000
to the home health agency.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.300
The patient suffered a broken hip eight weeks ago.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:18.900
Recent X-rays indicate to her physician that the bone is knitting satisfactorily,

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:24.100
and that the patient, Mrs. Lowe, will soon be ready for discharge from the hospital.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:30.000
[ Music ]

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:34.800
The attending physician informs Mrs. Lowe and her niece of the good news.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:41.700
But before setting a final departure date, the doctor conducts an evaluation conference on her case.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:48.360
With him are the hospital nursing supervisor, public health nursing coordinator, social worker,

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:52.140
and the physical therapist who has been working with Mrs. Lowe.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:59.000
[Doctor:] Do you feel satisfied from a physical therapy standpoint then, that Mrs. Lowe has made satisfactory progress?

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:02.740
[Physical Therapist:] Yes. Mrs. Lowe is ambulating very well with the stationary walker.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:07.020
[Narrator:] The physical therapist reports that the patient's progress has been good.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:11.000
But that she will need to continue walking exercise under supervision.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:17.900
[ Music ]

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:22.000
Since other aspects of her case indicate satisfactory recovery,

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.340
the doctor can order Mrs. Lowe's discharge.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:31.100
The physical therapist is instructed to demonstrate the walking exercise to the public health nurse assigned to the case.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:37.000
[ Music ]

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:41.280
The public health nurse will in turn supervise the home health aide.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.000
And make weekly checks of the patient's progress.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:52.000
With the services of the public health nurse and the home health aide available, Mrs. Lowe can look forward to going home.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:57.000
An early discharge is important to Mrs. Lowe and to the hospital.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:02.000
Where continuing care is available, the patient can recover at home,

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:06.140
and release a valuable hospital bed for a more critical case.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.280
Here, in the familiar surroundings of her own home,

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:17.260
Mrs. Lowe will receive assistance in her personal care as long as needed.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:25.660
Since she is over 65, the patient is eligible for Medicare, or health insurance for the aged under the Social Security Act.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:31.000
[Public Health Nurse:] Well, now since you're over 65 years old, Medicare is going to help you.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.000
[Mrs. Lowe:] Oh, I'm so glad somebody's gonna to help me.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:39.000
Although my niece helps me so much. Then I have another daughter too that helps me.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:43.820
[Public Health Nurse:] Good. Well, since you are under Medicare, they help to pay your hospital bill.

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:46.300
[Mrs. Lowe:] Well, that's good. I'm glad to hear that.

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:53.000
[Public Health Nurse:] And in addition, your doctor has ordered a home health aide to come in here and give you daily care

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:56.860
for the things that you can't do by yourself.

00:04:56.860 --> 00:05:03.000
She'll be here shortly, and you can meet her. Here's a list of the things that she will be able to do for you.

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:06.700
[Doorbell ringing ]

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:15.440
[Narrator:] The Home health aide is the newest member of the medical team.

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:23.600
Her job is to extend personal care to a patient at home, working under the supervision of a public health nurse.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:30.400
[Mrs. Lowe:] Yes, I was so glad that you've come and help me do a little of my ironing. My ironing...

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:34.740
[ Music ]

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:38.200
[Narrator:] The home health aide will call on Mrs. Lowe every weekday.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:41.000
On weekends the patient's niece will care for her.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:48.100
The niece, too, will do the shopping for food and other items necessary for her aunt's care.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:55.260
[ Music ]

00:05:55.320 --> 00:06:01.400
For the most part, the home health aide is concerned with direct personal care and safety of the patient.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:06.400
Her duties closely parallel those of a nurse's aide in a hospital or nursing home.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:10.960
Among these are assisting the patient in using the toilet or bedpan,

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:12.240
and in bathing.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:21.880
[ Music ]

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:26.100
The care of the patient's mouth, skin, and hair arek also duties of the aide.

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:31.000
But the home health aide is not a personal servant,

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:34.920
and she encourages the patient to care for herself whenever possible.

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:40.620
The patient's bedding is examined daily for cleanliness and comfort,

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:42.000
and changed if necessary.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:47.000
[ Music ]

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:50.500
While housekeeping is not normally a duty of a home health aide,

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:57.000
she may perform simple household tasks that relate directly to a healthful environment for the patient.

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:08.900
In this case, the aide's duties might include meal preparation since the patient lives alone and can stand or walk for only short periods.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:10.920
She cannot easily prepare balanced meals for herself.

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:16.580
Hot lunches are prepared daily.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:22.220
Casseroles and other dishes are made frequently since these may be easily reheated by the patient for dinner.

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:28.940
[ Music ]

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:31.400
Diets are prepared according to instructions from the doctor,

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:35.420
in keeping with the patient's personal likes and dislikes.

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:41.200
While it would be simple to serve the patient with a tray,

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:44.520
the aide urges her to seat herself at the table.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:50.200
It's one of the many steps towards self-sufficiency for the patient.

00:07:50.200 --> 00:08:06.160
[ Music ]

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:09.580
The aide is trained to observe patient condition and behavior.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:13.580
If a physical problem is noticed or if a patient complains,

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:17.920
the aide is instructed to call the nursing office at once.

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:24.880
The nursing supervisor will contact the public health nurse assigned to the case.

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:28.300
She in turn will report the problem to the patient's doctor.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:34.100
Here the problem is simple. Mrs. Lowe placed too much weight on her leg too soon.

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:45.000
[ Music ]

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:50.500
In each case, the public health nurse is the on-the-job supervisor of the home health aide.

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:58.800
The nurse, in turn, is carrying out the instructions of the attending physician and others on the medical team.

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:07.860
[ Music ]

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:14.100
The home health aide is authorized to carry out only those instructions which are issued by the public health nurse.

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:22.920
[ Music ]

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:25.200
[Home Health Aide:] Good morning, may I see the supervisor?

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:28.040
[Secretary:] Yes. Go right in. She's expecting you.

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:33.500
[Narrator:] Each week the home health aide has a brief meeting with her nursing supervisor.

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:35.300
[Home Health Aide:] Good morning.

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:42.340
[Nursing Supervisor:] Good morning. I've got your new schedule.

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:45.700
[Narrator:] The supervisor reviews the following week's schedule with the aide,

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:47.900
then discusses any problems which may have arisen.

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:52.700
[Home Health Aide:] Well, real well in a way. But she isn't eating too well.

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:55.920
[Nursing Supervisor:] She isn't? Are you having, does she eat when you're there?

00:09:55.920 --> 00:10:00.000
[Home Health Aide:] Yes, she eats when I'm there. But she won't fix it for herself.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:04.300
[Nursing Supervisor:] Maybe you ought to try that business that you did with Mr. Burnside.

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:10.100
When you brought him the TV trays and fixed a little bit of a complete meal on the TV tray and left it in the icebox for him.

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:10.780
Do you suppose?

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:14.400
[Home Health Aide:] That might work real well. That way she can just put that in the oven and...

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:18.740
[Nursing Supervisor:] She wouldn't have to spend time walking around that way.

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:21.820
Might be a good idea.

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:23.800
Make your emergency visits, and you found out that...

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:28.400
[Narrator:] The nursing supervisor holds periodic meetings with her home health aide staff.

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:31.300
Here she distributes helpful printed material,

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:35.700
and can describe new policies and developments which affect home health aides.

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:40.120
[Nursing Supervisor:] Well, what did you think about the book that we used?

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:41.280
[Home Health Aide:] I liked it very much.

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:43.300
[Nursing Supervisor:] Did you like it?  [Aide:] Uh-huh.

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:45.000
[Supervisor:] Did you get a good chance to use it?

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:45.760
[Home Health Aide:] Yes, I did.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:48.180
[Nursing Supervisor:] I heard you talking about the book this week. What did you think of it?

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:53.200
[Home Health Aide 2:] Well, I think it's very good. Especially this, uh, here with that one patient of mine.

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:56.500
He can't get up out of the bottom of the bathtub when he. ..

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:58.400
[Supervisor] Oh, this is that chair business, isn't it?

00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:01.020
[Home Health Aide 2:] She puts the chair in the bathtub as of now,

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:03.900
but she's going to get one of the other ones that is demonstrated in the book.

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:07.900
[Nursing Supervisor:] Mrs. Vaca, you took the book out to your arthritic patient the other day, didn't you?

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:11.000
[Mrs. Vaca:] No. This is the first time I have the book.

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:17.380
[Narrator:] The staff meeting serves as a forum too, where aides can raise questions, exchange information.

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:27.000
[Home Health Aide 3:] Well, last time I didn't get to use these gadgets because the patient I have is an arthritic

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:33.280
and she, I had to get in the shower with her. And put on one of those plastic raincoats that cover your head and all,

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:37.100
and take off my shoes and socks. Boy, that was really an experience.

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:40.600
[Nursing Supervisor:] Well, I'm glad you can laugh about it.

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:45.280
I think some of the new class of home health aides that we're training right now would be interested

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:47.700
in hearing some of these experiences.

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:51.560
They will be soon ready to go out on observation visits with some of you,

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:54.560
and I will be arranging for these with you.

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.180
[Instructor:] The public health nurse will be going in first.

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:59.400
[Narrator:] Good home health aides don't just happen.

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:02.500
They are carefully selected and trained.

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:09.640
The advantages and disadvantages, the responsibilities and the rewards of the job, must be made clear.

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:13.620
[Instructor:] With the public health nurse to plan what you can do for...

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:17.260
[Narrator:] The good home health aide is an emotionally mature person.

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:22.500
Perhaps one who has raised a family. They get satisfaction from working with people.

00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:27.400
And they are patient and understanding with the sick and their families.

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:31.280
[Instructor:] You would ask her any questions that you would have about the care of the patient.

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:36.100
[Instructor:] Another thing is the activities of daily living to make the patient.

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:43.500
[Narrator:] As training progresses, the student aides are given lectures and demonstrations by qualified members of the medical team.

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:49.300
[Instructor:] Use the long handled shoehorn for a patient without full flexion of his body or full use of his extremities.

00:12:49.900 --> 00:12:52.300
It enables him to put on his shoes by himself.

00:12:52.300 --> 00:12:56.880
[Instructor:] She isn't having any support here where the bend is in the bed.

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:59.500
[Narrator:] Students take turns playing the part of the patient.

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:04.360
Whenever possible, the demonstration simulate actual conditions.

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:11.000
[Background sounds ]

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:19.000
[Instructor:] To help them walk to a chair...It's best to help them sit on the edge of the bed first so that you can help them get their robe on.,

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:20.800
and help slip on their slippers.

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:27.000
Then to help them slide out and give them support as they walk.

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:31.000
[Another instructor:] Help the patient with their soup. If you dip it up and then run your spoon across.

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:36.380
[Narrator:] With the cooperation of a hospital or nursing home, students can practice with special equipment.

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:46.020
[Instructor:] Now if you'll try one. You don't want to have it too full either.

00:13:46.020 --> 00:13:50.000
[Instructor showing slides:] You can see the nurse trying to move the patient over in the bed,

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:55.380
and you can see that she stands quite close to 
the bed, has her back quite straight.

00:13:57.180 --> 00:14:03.100
In this slide, it demonstrates even more so why she uses this position and the value of this position.

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:13.900
[Instructor holding food:] Or a patient may have cheese. It can be a hard cheese or cottage cheese.

00:14:14.900 --> 00:14:19.600
[Narrator:] In an effective home health aide training program, study materials are plentiful,

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:22.500
and students are expected to read and 
understand them.

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:41.000
[ Rustling paper and other classroom sounds ]

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:44.800
Students are tested and evaluated during their training program.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:49.900
Successful completion of a course gives a trainee confidence in herself,

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:54.260
and justifiable pride in what she has learned and earned.

00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:59.100
Her effort may be rewarded by a certificate of completion or a badge.

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:09.160
[Instructor:] Mrs. Dishmon, congratulations.

00:15:10.460 --> 00:15:12.020
[Mrs. Dishmon:] Thank you very much.

00:15:13.940 --> 00:15:15.000
[Instructor:] Mr. Kingman.

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:18.900
[Public Health Nurse:] The man we're going to see now is a stroke patient.

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:22.000
He's progressing nicely now, but you should have seen.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:28.300
[Narrator:] After she has been employed by an agency, each new aide should have the opportunity to observe work in the field.

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:32.200
Often a public health nurse will conduct this orientation tour.

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:41.040
A lone invalid unable to care for himself is equally unable to care for his living quarters.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:16:02.000
[ Music ]

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:04.700
The results of neglect are often unpleasant.

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:06.400
Sometimes shocking.

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:14.700
So one of the first jobs of the aide is restoring a healthful environment,

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:17.400
and the rewards can be gratifying.

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:23.600
[ Music ]

00:16:24.280 --> 00:16:29.800
In the past months this patient has made a marked improvement through the teamwork of his doctor,

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:35.100
the occupational therapist, the public health nurse and the home health aide.

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:45.000
A rehabilitation program, guided by the occupational therapist, has enabled this patient to learn to perform simple tasks for himself.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:51.800
[ Music]

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:55.100
Complete recovery may not be possible for this patient.

00:16:55.560 --> 00:16:58.100
He will always require some personal help.

00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:05.200
But his newfound self-sufficiency has postponed the day when he needs full-time care in a nursing home.

00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:14.600
[ Music ]

00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:17.100
[Public Health Nurse:] There's a lady with multiple sclerosis.

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:19.560
We've been caring for her about a year and a half,

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:25.680
and you'll find she's a very interesting patient, really wanting to help herself do as much as she can.

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:31.000
But she has a husband who works during the week and a girl who goes to school.

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:35.500
So, therefore, she's left alone most of the time. We go in and help her.

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:37.400
[Mrs. Dishmon] How long has she been like this?

00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:38.620
[Public Health Nurse:] Several years now.

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:42.240
[ Murmuring ]

00:17:42.300 --> 00:17:44.860
Though sometimes she can get close enough to the table...

00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:50.100
[Narrator:] Not all cases handled by the home health aide involve the care of the elderly under Medicare.

00:17:50.120 --> 00:17:53.920
Like the public health nurses, her caseload will vary.

00:17:54.160 --> 00:17:59.120
As a rule, a doctor will request the need for the service of a home health aide

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:03.600
when there are no family members present who can give care to the patient.

00:18:04.280 --> 00:18:11.500
Fees for home health aide service are handled on a partial or full payment scale similar to fees for public health nurses.

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:15.040
Some health insurance plans absorb part of this cost.

00:18:15.300 --> 00:18:23.500
[ Music ]

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:32.700
The aide must understand how much assistance and what kind of assistance to give to the patient to help her maintain self-reliance.

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:42.300
[ Music ]

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:48.000
In each case, the duties of the home health aide are clearly outlined and scheduled.

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:52.160
At no time does the aide give care which has not been prescribed.

00:18:52.160 --> 00:19:00.000
[ Music ]

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:03.100
The student aide is learning firsthand about these responsibilities.

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:11.540
Soon she'll be given assignments where she'll make her own contributions as a part of the medical team.

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:22.300
[ Music ]

00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:25.500
For the others, the work goes on. Often to a happy ending.

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:32.800
Mrs. Lowe, for example, has recovered satisfactorily at home.

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:37.500
In a short time, her physician will terminate the services of the home health aide.

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:40.100
The aide's role has been important.

00:19:42.100 --> 00:19:48.200
Providing personal care, the valuable link between the patient and medical care personnel.

00:19:48.940 --> 00:19:54.100
Properly utilized, her skills will broaden the availability of medical service and care,

00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:58.800
and will give greater scope and flexibility to the other members of the medical team.

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:04.680
[ Music ]

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:11.600
Dedication. Service. Responsibility. This is the home health aide.

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:21.300
[ Music ]

